},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"74e6938570db388aaef153185e8c940ed4248bec81b695f8ae841139030f31ee","compact":"f0dcce408ebed3e8ee6e17e0e3f1d413cafef059becbf3a7c7b1d576296ca8ed","nasal":"f0dcce408ebed3e8ee6e17e0e3f1d413cafef059becbf3a7c7b1d576296ca8ed"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-1-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":1,"verse":15,"english":"He was aye of quiescent soul; and always precluded his speech with an amiable phrase; and although he might be addressed in a harsh manner, yet he returned no corresponding reply.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.953,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-1-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2001015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0da13ceab889f7f2928c683bcb3f499ef4ace7ba3d6c9a81e8381f6fd42ee161","compact":"5bffa6e37aab14f316be7ca4c811a1b483e2a13b6c4444bb0094387ca7b45aca","nasal":"ffd2a683139e116eb106ebafff264c306203ffd83901e1534f3e793d9b19a69b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-1-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":1,"verse":16,"english":"He was gratified even with a solitary instance of benefit; and from freedom of soul did not remember an hundred injuries.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.944,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-1-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2001016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"56fbcf5830deb18e9be72952db643f2d7bc70e8b04a3a2cb7bf6baf223870e4d","compact":"a34cb577632539496d4fb83c45cf7b805a86e5cced8f0f33c75219fbde586171","nasal":"a34cb577632539496d4fb83c45cf7b805a86e5cced8f0f33c75219fbde586171"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-1-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":1,"verse":17,"english":"In the intervals of martial exercises, he always discoursed with persons of character, or wise men, or the aged, or the virtuous.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-1-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2001017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d424d47ba1f1219599e62962fb0dc475c5204fd08cf291bc18fed279f2f87182","compact":"2ddcf0bd4079dc81b68e4e6771678581feb03f3d2d9d4202dac83f34414f1544","nasal":"6f153708f969d7bc117405296c024d03c219e9717ccb9027a6a6db087c49f0f0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-1-18","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":1,"verse":18,"english":"And he was the spring of all good; and was saintly; and of undisturbed soul; and truthtelling; and candid; and humble towards the aged twice-born ones cognisant of virtue and interest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-1-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2001018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7f8fb0e64164cc79934155868cbebd7b184d4a1f13735b2607d1bb54e217f964","compact":"628567e33193b32857fbf9047c1c7c3f8a204d0438e7561f235fb54b7fabcd69","nasal":"628567e33193b32857fbf9047c1c7c3f8a204d0438e7561f235fb54b7fabcd69"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-1-19","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":1,"verse":19,"english":"He was cognizant of virtue, profit, and interest; had an excellent memory; and was possessed of genius. He was an adept and was well versed in social usages and customs.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.578,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-1-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2001019","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8aac921aa36715b57d8922823972f00d0c500bb5e5e8b4f3352decf94c9b6616","compact":"eff63b30d96ba801d9d30da8a9c489ba28be3165e58c8c7ecc25129a0dc31c45","nasal":"eff63b30d96ba801d9d30da8a9c489ba28be3165e58c8c7ecc25129a0dc31c45"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-1-20","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":1,"verse":20,"english":"He was conversant with the scriptures; and was grateful; and could read the hearts of others. He had sagacity to perceive the seasons for duly showing favour or disfavour. are","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-1-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2001020","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c86e1c82404b787eecf510cb813df227ced890ddbc0a909ac5bc68136ad64fa4","compact":"0028e7c621a4ace9ab6d6d19f0ed3b9297a372d189e95b79ca16459b3f423b09","nasal":"808b14de2a37d2282f7c80f2560ce85ab745c30f10453603b1e96f71009237f7"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-1-21","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":1,"verse":21,"english":"He understood all about the reception of the righteous, the maintenance of family, and the occasion for chastising, evil-doers; and he was an expert in collecting dues (from the people;) and knew the manner prescribed (by the authorities) for expending money. He had attained proficiency in all the scriptures and literary works composed in both Sanskrit and Prakrit. He sought pleasure without sacrificing either interest or morality; and he was never dilatory in duty.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.377,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-1-25","DUTT-2-1-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2001021","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"167a66772d5b49a617de13041e6983035878deded9adbc083a4c23acb1339c05","compact":"a296b561e6a1b01977a6918bb761523e779f143ff3727e90dc6b530960ea82cd","nasal":"a296b561e6a1b01977a6918bb761523e779f143ff3727e90dc6b530960ea82cd"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-1-22","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":1,"verse":22,"english":"He had attained proficiency in all the scriptures and literary works composed in both Sanskrit and Prakrit. He sought pleasure without sacrificing either interest or morality; and he was never dilatory in duty. He understood the of those who entertained others. He knew the various heads on which wealth was to be expended. He was skilful in riding and training up horses and elephants.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-1-26","DUTT-2-1-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2001022","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ad1976a6269c129f4730d0b5b2920edbc5ea16c9340b045425623958e6bf3c56","compact":"b0447e3f15aba59778b37073af9a41f179ee8ea2ed794ed448411c5ed6120742","nasal":"f7557a03a857af155855e6926f2d4befa95ceb1f462be5ad3a95d71ae10185b4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-1-23","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":1,"verse":23,"english":"He understood the of those who entertained others. He knew the various heads on which wealth was to be expended. He was skilful in riding and training up horses and elephants. He was the foremost of those accomplished in archery; and was acknowledged among men as an Atiratha. * He led his forces in the direction of the foe; and he slew his enemies; and was accomplished in marshalling the troops. *He who alone vanquishes an innumerable host of warriors is called an Atiratha.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.414,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-1-27","DUTT-2-1-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2001023","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"788626e82a74f7151e3fa340488a3d30b3af2c1e04e59f1c8f6874f42a009eee","compact":"3f0dbc835606650dca6497f82d06bb8906458195d3bb8cb566faf47f74eb60ca","nasal":"3f0dbc835606650dca6497f82d06bb8906458195d3bb8cb566faf47f74eb60ca"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-1-24","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":1,"verse":24,"english":"He was the foremost of those accomplished in archery; and was acknowledged among men as an Atiratha. * He led his forces in the direction of the foe; and he slew his enemies; and was accomplished in marshalling the troops. *He who alone vanquishes an innumerable host of warriors is called an Atiratha. He was incapable of being repressed in fight even by the enraged gods and Asuras. He was not given to carping, and had subdued his anger, and he was never elated, or malicious.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.532,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-1-28","DUTT-2-1-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2001024","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a84aff4d1f466cbcf09e90cd893eed6269492a435b7f7b67c7f727b093e01a33","compact":"caf42acdea9f509386a8f167c903a9371aae855099e9706f81419be42aa7dd6a","nasal":"caf42acdea9f509386a8f167c903a9371aae855099e9706f81419be42aa7dd6a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-1-25","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":1,"verse":25,"english":"He was incapable of being repressed in fight even by the enraged gods and Asuras. He was not given to carping, and had subdued his anger, and he was never elated, or malicious.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.275,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-1-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2001025","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"74ed31d590553093c6c74d5217d40dd4ec7f1cddc6fcb6aa715aef0bac5b2f0d","compact":"fee13698a52085617ff45e4bb53e0e2ebaeab51d4f52fa28b8a865201603d0ed","nasal":"610bd5e92b6f93f280bda2b74a73a3866a58608834ad368f37dd9747d7a6db4e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-1-26","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":1,"verse":26,"english":"He did not disregard any creature; he was no slave to the times. That son of the monarch was furnished with such qualities. And he was liked by the subjects as well as by the three worlds. In forgiveness he was like to the Earth; and in intelligence like to BỊhaspati; and in prowess like to the Sacī's lord.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskr