any incomparable qualities, that subduer of his enemies, king Dasaratha, thought within himself.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-1-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2001029","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8fb938a0a21e6c25f095f592d0fd53c40db22922c28b50ea33de1f48e36ca82b","compact":"d26f80d788a70b486ba2757bc0e30e4231c487ce72c8c66bba1abaece8b19b23","nasal":"9c4b7f452ceabde2f562cc53cc6582a8d495c42e4bdd0cafe85c2e49e8470fe7"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-1-30","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":1,"verse":30,"english":"Surely he always wished for the prosperity of the people; and he showed kindness to all creatures. And like to the showering rain-cloud, he is dearer to the people than myself.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.821,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-1-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2001030","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cb51bfc923af97d1212c8a0c8682ec63e93f6ce44c3a74e4f3c304b998662d2f","compact":"d19f4e161bbe622009016a430993653a85a54ecf15226ba2d5b154acd5e64dfd","nasal":"d19f4e161bbe622009016a430993653a85a54ecf15226ba2d5b154acd5e64dfd"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-1-31","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":1,"verse":31,"english":"Surely he always wished for the prosperity of the people; and he showed kindness to all creatures. And like to the showering rain-cloud, he is dearer to the people than myself.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-1-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2001031","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c32280e5ee06ae99fdef16645ae84949fa932dd7215b3febcd7f8532908238e3","compact":"40dd48d8422975474bbee1167782e9c6df0f886c6809a015ccd5cf6df1aa1